SYMBOLIC_CHAIN_SEALED
S1 [source-derived, VoR 102-203]: ECKS gives local field equations (3)-(6).
S2 [source-derived, VoR 204-406]: spin conservation gives multipole identity (17).
S3 [source-derived, VoR 551-568]: Eq. (33) is only order-of-magnitude:
   m/r_C^3 ~ (G/c^4)(hbar/r_C^3)^2.
   Therefore r_C^3 ~ G hbar^2/(m c^4), r_C proportional to m^(-1/3),
   and rho_C=m/r_C^3 is proportional to m^2.
S4 [source-derived, VoR 625-653]: rho_Ce is an expected approximate ceiling;
   extension from particles to self-gravitating systems is expressly conjectural.
S5 [source-derived, VoR 662-664]: rho_BH <= rho_Ce and ~10^16 kg are asserted.
THEOREM TEST: a density ceiling alone has no mass dimension and implies no M floor
unless a source-bound relation supplies a length/volume as a function of mass.
FAILED_BINDING_ATTEMPT_1: the source does not define rho_BH as a local scalar or
a proper-volume average; coordinate-volume and Euclidean-volume readings are unlicensed.
FAILED_BINDING_ATTEMPT_2: the source defines no black-hole mass notion, trapped-surface
radius relation, interior profile, charge/spin domain, or interior/exterior matching map.
FIRST_UNBOUND_QUANTITY: V(M), equivalently a source-bound size/mass relation.
STOPPING_RULE: two failed attempts to bind the same missing global premise.
CONCLUSION: no source-bound theorem rho <= rho_Ce => M >= M_min > 0 is reproduced
from the stated inputs; this is not a claim that the printed statement is an error.
C2 control: unit-coefficient r_Ce=4.655097e-28 m; log10=-27.332071.
C3 symbolic: R=2GM/c^2 and V=4pi R^3/3 imply rho_bar=3c^6/(32piG^3M^2).
C3 numerical probe printed by script: M=2.500000e+16 kg, rho=1.165865e+47 kg/m^3.
ADDED_COMPLETION_CONTROL: Schwarzschild/Euclidean/uniform-mean floor=2.699381e+14 kg.
COMPLETION_CHANGE_CONTROL: radius coefficient 3 gives floor=1.469357e+14 kg.
C5 deletion: deleting source ECKS equations leaves the injected GR control floor intact;
therefore that relation is circular for K6 and no derived-floor class is allowed.
C6 split: changing an added size/mass completion changes the floor, exposing dependence.
